Package: noqtis
Type: Package
Title: Post-Quantum Signing, Key Encapsulation and Sealed Folders
Version: 0.1.3
Authors@R: c(
    person(c("Vansh", "Singh"), "Ruhela", email = "vsruhela@proton.me",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0004-1750-3592", GitHub = "rootcoder007")))
Description: A post-quantum cryptography toolkit for R, built on the
    dependency-free 'NOQTIS' C library. Generate key pairs, then sign and
    verify with lattice-based 'ML-DSA', hash-based 'SLH-DSA', 'Ed25519' or
    hybrid 'ML-DSA'+'Ed25519' signatures that need both halves to verify;
    establish shared secrets with 'ML-KEM' or 'HQC' key encapsulation; and
    hash with 'SHA-2', 'SHA-3' or 'SHAKE', with 'HMAC'. A whole directory
    can be sealed under one signature and later verified offline; a
    Merkle proof shows chosen files to someone without revealing the
    others, and signed statements rotate or revoke a sealing key. Results
    can be wrapped in 'DSSE' envelopes. Keys and nonces come from the
    operating system's random generator, not from R's.
